== Problem 3 (changed rule: move the larger of today's two new cards)
ok   the larger new card is 2n; it moves on its entry day
ok   changed rule: A_n = odd labels 1..2n-1, B_n = even labels 2..2n (overview)
ok   end-of-day count histories identical under both rules
ok   mid-day count histories identical too (no count at any moment tells the rules apart)
ok   the card arrangements differ on every day n >= 1
ok   day 1 already shows it: A = {1} (changed) vs A = {2} (smallest)
ok   one-card witness: card 1 is in B under the smallest rule and in A under the changed rule on every day >= 1
== Problem 4 (eventual membership)
ok   smallest rule: label k last changes on day k and stays in B to day 1500 (k = 1..600)
ok   changed rule: label k last changes on day ceil(k/2); odd -> A, even -> B (k = 1..600)
ok   smallest rule, every day N >= 1: label N+1 is in A, so A is never empty after day 0 (guide witness)
ok   smallest rule, day 0: A empty but B empty too (guide: day 0 is not the arrangement)
ok   both rules: a finite day holds only 2N labels, so "all labels settled" never appears in full
ok   smallest rule: no day 1..299 has every present card in its settled bowl (N+1..2N sit in A)
ok   changed rule: on EVERY day each card present is already in its settled bowl (A odds, B evens) -- a child reading "that arrangement" as "odds in A, evens in B" can truthfully answer yes
