== Guide p. 4 adult analysis
ok   a_n(k) = 0 for all n >= k: pointwise limit 0
ok   sum_k a_n(k) = n -> infinity
ok   sup_k a_n(k) = 1 for every n >= 1 and 0 for n = 0 (guide)
ok   sup_n a_n(k) = 1 for every k >= 2: the least majorant is not summable (guide: no summable majorant)
ok   B_n is increasing (monotone membership), |B_n| = n
ok   support for "nonuniformity alone is not a universal explanation": 1/n on k <= n converges uniformly to 0 yet sums to 1
